<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korean firms buy 15,000 tonnes of Indian soymeal.</title>
<headline>S.Korean firms buy 15,000 tonnes of Indian soymeal.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korean feedmill companies bought 15,000 tonnes of Indian soymeal at $302.50 a tonne, C&amp;F, traders said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The companies included Miwon Co Ltd, Purina Korea Inc, Cheiljedang Corp, and Taihan Sugar Corp.</p>
<p>South Korean trading house LG International Corp sold the soymeal with shipment for January 11-30 to the port city of Kunsan through private negotiations.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5651</p>
</text>
